Extract compound-string text with XmStringUnparse instead of XmStringGetLtoR.

Under the in-tree Motif built against libx11-compat, XmStringGetLtoR misbehaves
for an optimized compound string: it returns the segment tag
("FONTLIST_DEFAULT_TAG_STRING") instead of the text. Grace routes every
XmString-to-char conversion through GetStringSimple, so a filename picked in the
file selection box comes back as the tag and the file cannot be opened
("Can't stat file ..."). XmStringUnparse decodes the same string correctly; this
mirrors the established compat/gimp-patches XmStringUnparse workaround for the
identical GetLtoR defect.

--- a/src/motifutils.c
+++ b/src/motifutils.c
@@ -4156,13 +4156,14 @@
 
 char *GetStringSimple(XmString xms)
 {
-    char *s;
-
-    if (XmStringGetLtoR(xms, charset, &s)) {
-        return s;
-    } else {
-        return NULL;
-    }
+    /* XmStringGetLtoR returns the segment tag rather than the text for an
+     * optimized compound string under the libx11-compat Motif build, so a
+     * selected filename comes back as "FONTLIST_DEFAULT_TAG_STRING" and cannot
+     * be opened. XmStringUnparse decodes the same string correctly, matching the
+     * compat/gimp-patches XmStringUnparse workaround.
+     */
+    return XmStringUnparse(xms, NULL, XmCHARSET_TEXT, XmCHARSET_TEXT,
+                           NULL, 0, XmOUTPUT_ALL);
 }
 
 extern int ReqUpdateColorSel;
